# Git must not translate line endings anywhere in this repository.
#
# The reference sidecars under crates/psolve-cli/tests/fixtures/ are byte-exact
# copies of real astap_cli output, and sidecar_ini.rs / sidecar_wcs.rs compare
# psolve's own output against them byte for byte. That is the whole
# ASTAP-compatibility guarantee.
#
# Git's default core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites their LF to CRLF on
# checkout, so the tests then compare against fixtures that no longer match
# what astap_cli actually wrote -- and a passing run would be meaningless
# rather than merely absent. Measured 2026-08-27 on a windows-latest runner:
# two sidecar_ini tests failed with \r\n on the right-hand side.
#
# `-text` disables all EOL conversion for every path. It is deliberately
# repo-wide rather than fixture-scoped: nothing here wants CRLF, and a
# narrower rule would leave the next byte-exact fixture unprotected.
* -text

# Belt and braces for the binary artefacts, so no future setting can touch them.
*.psidx binary
*.psqidx binary
*.gz binary
*.wcs binary
*.ini binary
